  "dedup": [
    {
      "existing": "R1",
      "reason": "R1 (fake-verify-before-claim) targets verifying completion claims before reporting success; this incident is about delivering unrequested extra scope, a different failure mode.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R2",
      "reason": "R2 (Fake Release Discipline) is about running a verification command before reporting a fake release complete; unrelated to over-delivering beyond requested scope.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R3",
      "reason": "R3 (pending hook) addresses unconfirmed destructive deletes — a mechanically detectable, permission-gated action. This incident is about adding unrequested extra deliverables (a scope-size violation), which a hook cannot detect; different failure mode and different remedy shape.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R4",
      "reason": "R4 (pending claude-md) already covers violating an explicit scope/method constraint mid-task (e.g., do-not-touch, no-network). This incident's request implicitly bounded scope to a single file, and the agent exceeded it — the same underlying scope-deviation failure mode. Per merge bias, this revises R4 rather than creating a sibling proposal.",
      "verdict": "overlap"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "incident_id": 6,
      "quote": "That's not what I asked; the request was a one-file note."
    }
  ],
  "failure_statement": "Agent delivered more than the requested scope (added extra unrequested content/files) when the user explicitly asked for a single one-file note.",
  "overlap_action": {
    "revises": "proposal #2"
  },
  "remedy_content": {
    "target": "global",
    "text": "# Scope Discipline\n\nWhen the user specifies scope (e.g., \"just a one-file note,\" \"only fix X\"), deliver exactly that — no extra files, demos, or unrequested additions. If something beyond scope seems worth doing, mention it as a suggestion rather than including it in the deliverable.\n"
  },
  "remedy_type": "claude-md",
  "routing_rationale": "This is a plain scope-deviation: the user asked for a single-file note and got extra unrequested deliverables (their own words: \"That's not what I asked; the request was a one-file note\"). Nothing here requires multi-step procedure (ruling out skill) and there's no mechanical signal a hook could gate on before the fact (scope creep isn't a detectable file/command pattern, ruling out hook) — a one-line standing rule to deliver exactly what was asked and flag extras as suggestions rather than including them is sufficient and cheapest. R4 is an existing pending claude-md proposal already covering \"violating an explicit scope/method constraint mid-task\" — this incident is the same taxonomy failure (scope-deviation: did more than asked), so per merge bias this revises R4 rather than creating a sibling proposal.",
  "singleton": true
}

